Need body.in-heist .mobile-nav hide at <=900. Add there. Also view padding bottom reduce for heist. And CTA hidden in heist via .is-on false (canPromo false), fine.

Add mobile-specific in @media 900. Better in responsive.css near mobile block. Also heist reorder.

Let's edit responsive.css @media(max-width:900px) adding body.in-heist. Since display grid rule at 900 (styles.css 683), specificity: body.in-heist .mobile-nav { display:none } higher.

Also for toast root bottom adjust when nav hidden? toast bottom remains 78px, not a big deal but can override body.in-heist .toast-root { bottom: calc(16px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)); }.

Now heist reorder at <=900? Mobile actions reachable at 760 or 560? At <=900 the nav appears; so reorder at <=900. But tablet 900 maybe two columns layout already 1fr at <=1060 with side 2 cols at 1060, then 1fr at 900. For 761-900, heist-side single column under main. Could reorder only <=760 to avoid weird desktop-tablet. But mobile nav at <=900. Actions below footer at 800px; okay. Use <=760 reorder, and body.in-heist nav hide at <=900. At 800 heist is still long but okay.

Actually mobile 390 is the concern. Use <=760.

CSS:
@media (max-width:760px) {
  .heist-grid { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 9px; }
  .heist-main, .heist-side { display: contents; }
  ... order
}
But `display:contents` on .heist-main removes its gap; all items gap 9. Order as desired. Note heist-grid also contains only those two wrappers. Great.

However .heist-main has `min-width:0` not issue.

Set:
.target-band { order:1; }
.map-panel { order:2; }
.action-panel { order:3; }
.alert-panel { order:4; }
.heist-chips { order:5; }
.heist-footer { order:6; }
